From 22a77378b2a0e672b1f4c5488ccf353ec51a98fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:50:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(input): Arbor stands in the path of a person's input
 only while they hold its keys
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A tap that has outlived the right to it costs the Mac its input at every event it asks for. On hosted
Macs one that is installed but switched off started nothing, and one that was switched on after the
right had gone started the drop that instant. Two of Arbor's four taps were on all day.

- All four taps are installed paused. Each goes on only while a gesture could be Arbor's: ⌥ down for the
  pinch, exactly ⌃⌥ for the scroll and the rectangle, or a gesture of Arbor's is in progress.
- No tap goes on but by a fresh yes of macOS's: whoever wants one on asks first, a third of a millisecond.
- The clock beats every 0.05 s while a tap is wanted on, and not at all otherwise.
- The time an answer may take is counted in beats, so a halt or a sleep uses up none of it.
- A pause from another thread switches the tap off from there first, and needs nothing of the taps' thread.
- ⇧-drag on the Desktop ships off, and the pinch without ⌥ over the Desktop is a setting now, off.
- Each setting that needs a tap on with none of Arbor's keys down says so in one line.
- Two sabotages for probes: the clock's timer ends, or the taps' thread comes to stand.

The macOS half type-checks on Linux and has not run on a Mac yet.
