From b434ef30920a31ca4723dd4f356a3f3855da4f65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:36:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(input): what a second read, of the mends alone, found
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- With every beat late the count of an answer's time began again at every beat, and patience was never lost.
  It begins again once for a question.
- Beats that had found no tap on were held against one that went on later. Only beats that find a tap on count.
- The owners asked the window server which keys are down from the taps' thread at every beat. They ask when
  macOS has just answered, and not while a question hangs.
- Two narrow races around a tap that the main thread has switched off, each ending in TapHealth counting
  Arbor's own switching off as macOS's.
- With `pinchOnDesktop` among the gestures every script asks for, the pinch tap and the clock ran all day, and no
  check on a Mac could tell whether the keys switch the taps. It is out again: whoever is about it asks for it.
- A ⌃⌥ scroll and a ⌃⌥ click from cold, with their effect checked, in input-taps.sh.
- Momentum is given up after eight beats without an event, not four: nobody has measured how long it can stall.
- One test whose premise could not arise is gone.
